eted":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n-Reproducible in 4.7.beta2 and later\n-Not reproducible in 4.7.beta1 and earlier\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.7.beta2.mono - Windows 10 (build 19045) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 4070 Ti (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.9174) - 13th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-13700K (24 threads) - 63.74 GiB memory - WASAPI (48000 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nLikely related:  [#118651](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118651)\n\nLabels with a maximum size and autowrap enabled will only ever grow to the right, regardless of which horizontal grow direction is set with its anchors.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Create a scene with a Label\n- Set the Label's anchors to be centered\n- Give the Label a maximum size of (100, 100)\n- Set the Label's autowrap mode to Arbitrary\n- Add enough text to the Label to cause its minimum size to grow\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[label_grow_direction_mrp.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/28813641/label_grow_direction_mrp.zip)\n\nOpening the scene in 4.7.beta1 will have the label centered, while opening it in 4.7.beta2 will have it shifted to the right.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repo